WHY THE FIRST COMPILER EMITS ASSEMBLY DIRECTLY.

Decision status: human correction accepted for the first executable slice,
2026-10-11. This file supersedes earlier suggestions to include ICK
in English Major C's translation stages.

THE PURPOSE.
English Major C is not an insult to English majors or an exercise
in describing simple programs for beginners. It makes an actual machine
more inspectable by replacing optional jargon, obscure abbreviations,
and metaphors with the ordinary English names of exact operations.
The machine's genuine complexity and constraints must remain visible.
Long names should explain rather than merely inflate a short name.
For example, "unknown entry" is sufficient where the first example
requires nothing more. "Missing integer" is preferable to
"missing value that is an integer" if an integer distinction
eventually becomes relevant.

THE FIRST TARGET.
One initial instruction set only: ARMv7-A T32 (Thumb), using the
machine and limited operation grant under arm/thumb/.
No second target, general target-independent intermediate representation,
universal source-language type system, or promise of portability
is required for this initial experiment.
The existing T32 specification is a draft contract for a symbolic
architecture, not measured evidence of a particular physical CPU.

THE FIRST COMPILER.
The project's own small, fixed-grammar compiler converts a permitted
English instruction sentence directly to an ARM T32 assembler instruction.
It explicitly names registers, instructions and control transfers.
No C compiler, ICK compiler, Idris frontend, R program, or extra
language translation stage is part of this English-to-assembly step.

The target assembler still encodes instruction bytes from assembly,
and a separate toolchain may later link and load them. Neither of those
is secretly a source-to-assembly implementation. For a maintained
Android target, use the independently declared Android NDK stage
and report its actual acceptance. The developer's diagnostic LLVM
cross-assembly does not equal that future evidence.

THINGS WE NEED NOT DECIDE YET.
Whether the eventual language has integers, floating-point values,
characters, a general missing-value abstraction, syntax for record
layouts, or a static type system. We must state each present machine
representation accurately, but a current representation is not by
itself the language's ontology.

In the first example, one all-ones 32-bit memory word simply means
"unknown" and is omitted from addition. A distinct validity word
and other approaches remain open. There is no requirement to model
R's NA and NaN, nor to accept every value an R integer vector can
contain.

WHAT THIS COMPILER DOES NOT CLAIM.
It is not yet a general English Major C parser, optimizer, Idris
frontend, machine-code assembler, operating-system loader, or
physical CPU interpreter. A direct assembly listing is evidence
of a compilation result, not execution of those instructions.

